\beta\tau\) does so, the amplitude \(H\) after ¶ \(n\) such changes of sign will be \[H = \frac{p}{\beta mk} (1 + e^{-\alpha\tau}) \cdot (1 + e^{-\alpha\tau} + e^{-2\alpha\tau} + \dots + e^{-n\alpha\tau})\] or @@A@@
