<<<
@@A@@
===
\[x = B \cdot e^{-\frac{b^2 t}{2m}} \cdot \sin (\nu t + c)\] where \[\nu = \frac{1}{m} \cdot \sqrt{(a^2 m - \tfrac{1}{4} b^2)}.\]

On account of the factor which contains \(t\) in the exponent, the value of \(x\) continually diminishes. As in the text, measure \(t\) by @@A@@
